public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "hello";
        char target = 'e';

        boolean found = false;

        for (int i = 0; i < str.length(); i++) {
            if (str.charAt(i) == target) {
                found = true;
                break;
            }
        }

        if (found) {
            System.out.println("Character found");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Character not found");
        }
    }
}

Understand: charAt(i) gives you the character at index i.

For "hello":
Index	Character
0	h
1	e
2	l
3	l
4	o
